    "propInertiaSource": "Propeller + spinner + the crank's rotating parts, kg.m2. From the OWNER'S BLADE RULE (2026-11-09, tools/aircraft_builder/prop_inertia.py): each blade is 15 % of the net propeller weight with its centre of mass at 25 % of the DIAMETER from the axis, the rest being hub near the axis - because a heavy constant-speed hub contributes almost nothing to sum(m r^2), so a mass-weighted estimate overstates the couple. M 20.0 kg, D 1.88 m, 2 blades: blades 1.325 + hub 0.140 (k 0.10 m) + crank 0.09 = 1.56, against 3.5 before. MASS: SOURCED: Sensenich give 44 lb for the metal Super Cub propeller. O-320, four cylinders. VALIDATION: the rule reproduces Hartzell's published two-blade polar moment to +18 % (1.412 against 1.198) and runs +60 % high on their three-blade one, so it is applied to two-blade types only.",
